course: dictionary
lesson: 10116
title: Same word, different places
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The same word can mean different things in different places. Context, the words and places around a word, gives you the clue. «In Australia "thongs" means flip-flops», so the country tells you which meaning to pick.
explain: «Grab your togs and thongs» is said in Sydney. Togs is a clue: it means swimsuit, so thongs must mean flip-flops, not underwear. Always ask which meaning fits the words around it.
explain: Check by swapping your meaning into the sentence. Flip-flops fits the beach sentence. In history, «a thong» tied shoes and tools, so a thin strip of leather fits there. Only one meaning will make sense each time.
fact: Thong has more than one meaning: flip-flops, a piece of underwear or swimwear, or a thin strip of leather.
fact: In Australia and New Zealand, «thongs» means flip-flops. In New Zealand, people also say jandals.
fact: In the UK and USA, thong often means a piece of underwear, so the word can cause funny mix-ups between countries.
fact: «Togs» means swimsuit in Australia, and «arvo» means afternoon.
fact: A thong is a thin strip of leather used to tie or fasten things.
exercise: «Grab your togs and thongs» is said in Sydney. What are thongs here? | Sunhats | *Flip-flops | A thin strip of leather | Long socks
exercise: Which clue in «Grab your togs and thongs» tells you thongs means flip-flops? | The word Sydney, meaning a city | The word grab, meaning take quickly | The word your, meaning belonging to you | *The word togs, meaning swimsuit
exercise: In history, people tied shoes with a leather thong. What is a thong here? | A pair of flip-flops | A sandal from Sydney | *A thin strip of leather | A swimsuit
test: «Turn left at the robot» is said in Cape Town. What does robot mean here? | *A traffic light | A type of sandal | A wet, grey day | A toy machine that walks and talks
test: In New Zealand, what do people call flip-flops? | Thongs | Robots | *Jandals | Togs
exam: Why can the word thong mean different things in different countries? | Because thongs are always made of leather | Because maps are often wrong | Because the word is too long to read | *Because the same word can mean different things in each place
